[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent Circuit Consistency Audits

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This bounded audit profile supplements numerical residuals with element-level physical checks. Passing checks establish consistency within recorded tolerances, not model validity, uniqueness, global waveform accuracy or production qualification. Iterations 311-320 implement this profile; broader sparse, model and ngspice qualification remains active.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-001
TITLE: Explicit bounded audit evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Audits shall expose passed, failed and not_checked outcomes with SI discrepancy, effective tolerance and a reason when unavailable. Invalid tolerance settings shall be rejected and nonfinite check arithmetic shall fail with JSON-safe null metrics.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs Check, AuditOptions and AuditReport. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::audit_metrics_are_json_safe_and_bounds_are_validated.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-002
TITLE: Independent DC current conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC audit shall reconstruct supported element currents without assembled matrices or production model evaluation, check KCL at every node including ground, and reject malformed or nonfinite MNA states. Fixed Gmin shall be explicitly included with unregularized physics marked not_checked.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::dc and dc_currents. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::independent_kcl_detects_perturbed_current_and_rejects_malformed_states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-003
TITLE: Independent voltage constraints
STATEMENT: >>>
The DC audit shall check independent voltage sources, VCVS, CCVS and DC inductor voltage constraints separately from KCL using voltage-dimensional bounds. A KCL-consistent state violating an ideal voltage source shall fail.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::constraint_checks. Verification: tests/consistency.rs voltage_constraint_catches_a_kcl_consistent_wrong_solution and controlled_voltage_and_inductor_constraints_are_audited.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-004
TITLE: DC power conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The independent DC audit shall sum absorbed element power using passive sign convention and include explicit Gmin dissipation. It shall report a power-dimensional absolute-plus-relative bound and fail nonfinite arithmetic. Shunt-regularized success shall not imply an unregularized physical solution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::power_check. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::power_audit_includes_shunt_dissipation_and_detects_wrong_source_current.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-005
TITLE: Bounded topology preflight
STATEMENT: >>>
Preflight shall identify directly conflicting parallel independent voltage sources with polarity normalization and warn about nodes lacking an obvious DC reference path. Connectivity warnings shall not reject explicitly initialized transient or controlled-source circuits. Diagnostics shall have stable codes, severity and affected identifiers; complete rank or DAE classification is outside this profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/topology.rs. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::topology_warns_about_capacitor_only_paths_and_identifies_source_conflicts.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-006
TITLE: Backward-Euler physical step audit
STATEMENT: >>>
For finite complete MNA states and positive timesteps with constant nominal sources, the audit shall independently check capacitor current, inductor voltage, KCL, source constraints and discrete energy balance. The energy identity shall include backward-Euler numerical dissipation, not assert exact continuous energy conservation. Waveform aggregation shall retain the worst normalized discrepancy per check with memory bounded by circuit size.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::backward_euler_step and AuditReport::merge_worst. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::backward_euler_energy_audit_includes_integration_dissipation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-007
TITLE: Public audit and diagnostic evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Successful API manifests shall include bounded preflight diagnostics and independent consistency checks. DC and legacy constant-source backward-Euler transient states shall be audited before derived signals are appended; failed physical checks shall return numerical_failure. AC/configured transient physical audits and global accuracy shall be explicitly not_checked. C# consumers shall receive typed additive result fields.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/api.rs and dotnet/Simulator.Client/Results.cs. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::manifests_distinguish_physical_checks_and_unavailable_evidence and dotnet/Simulator.Conformance/Program.cs typed audit checks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-008
TITLE: Structured opt-in diagnostic logging
STATEMENT: >>>
Rust library code shall emit structured tracing events without installing a global subscriber. The CLI shall install a JSON stderr subscriber filtered by RUST_LOG with warn fallback and leave stdout as protocol JSON only. Events shall identify request/backend context, topology diagnostics, compilation size, audit completion, and bounded continuation stages; Newton iteration residuals shall require trace level. Events shall not dump raw netlists, solution vectors or whole requests.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/main.rs, src/api.rs and src/newton.rs; tracing and tracing-subscriber versions are locked in Cargo.lock. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::debug_logging_keeps_protocol_stdout_clean.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-009
TITLE: Explicit timestep-refinement comparison
STATEMENT: >>>
The Rust audit API shall compare independently supplied coarse and finer waveforms for a selected voltage or current at exactly shared coarse times, rejecting malformed axes, nonfinite values, missing signals or mismatched stop times. It shall retain the worst normalized discrepancy and identify observed change as distinct from a rigorous global accuracy bound. It shall not silently rerun the solver or interpolate samples.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/audit.rs::compare_refinement. Verification: tests/consistency.rs::timestep_refinement_compares_shared_samples_without_claiming_global_accuracy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: CONS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CONS-010
TITLE: Reproducible audit qualification and limits
STATEMENT: >>>
The audit slice shall retain independent analytic examples, corrupted-state and loose-Newton rejection, malformed-state fuzz-smoke and seeded properties, targeted isolated mutations, full checkpoint checks and actual coverage availability. Reported evidence shall distinguish physical consistency from global accuracy and model validity, and identify unsupported analysis profiles and instrumentation limitations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/consistency.rs, scripts/Mutation.cs, evidence/checkpoint-320.json and evidence/consistency-qualification.md. Authoritative runtime requirements are CONS-001 through CONS-009; this requirement does not infer complete M1 qualification.
<<<
