[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-001
TITLE: Bounded isolated endurance campaign
STATEMENT: >>>
A manual endurance target shall run a selected mutation campaign once, then changing-seed endurance batches within a configurable monotonic wall-clock budget capped at 24 hours with a five-hour default. It shall use an isolated source snapshot, reject overlapping supervised runs through an exclusive file lock, cap child-process runtimes and retained logs, and report completed cases separately from partial, timed-out or failed work. Compiler/test concurrency shall be bounded. Working source and tracked qualification reports shall not be modified by a campaign.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Makefile, scripts/Endurance.cs and scripts/Run-Endurance.ps1. Verification: tests/Endurance.Tests.ps1 and evidence/endurance-qualification.md. OS-wide memory enforcement and cleanup after forced supervisor termination are not claimed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-002
TITLE: Reproducible changing-seed endurance evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
The endurance harness shall explore bounded parser mutations, sparse layouts, independent analytic divider solutions and diode derivative cases using recorded seeds. Reports shall retain source hashes, revision/dirty state, tool versions, completed-case counts and replay seeds. Failure inputs shall be preserved, with bounded deletion minimization for parser panics. Each source archive shall remain available after later runs; interrupted work shall never be called passing or covered.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: tests/endurance.rs and scripts/Endurance.cs. Verification: manual deterministic seed replay, budget and overlap checks in evidence/endurance-qualification.md. This is seeded fuzz/property testing, not coverage-guided fuzzing or an exhaustive source-mutation campaign.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-003
TITLE: Nightly invocation and morning evidence review
STATEMENT: >>>
The user-authorized scheduled workflow shall start a hidden five-hour-budget campaign at local midnight and review its actual artifacts at 05:05 America/Los_Angeles. Startup and results review shall distinguish active, missing, failed, unfinished and budget-exhausted work; a configured schedule shall not be treated as an executed five-hour qualification run.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: local thread automations spice-nightly-endurance-campaign and spice-morning-endurance-results, invoking scripts/Run-Endurance.ps1. Verification: saved automation configurations and the hidden-worker startup checks retained in evidence/endurance-qualification.md. Local machine/app availability is required; the initial full overnight execution remains pending.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REM-001
TITLE: Configurable cross-host qualification bootstrap
STATEMENT: >>>
The qualification workflow shall accept a finite positive endurance budget up to 24 hours, defaulting to five hours, and provide PowerShell setup for Windows x64 and Ubuntu/Debian x64. It shall read pinned SDK/compiler/documentation-tool versions, configure process-local tool paths, use official installer sources and record acquisition hashes. Required administrator approval and private-repository authentication shall remain explicit prerequisites, not silently bypassed. Setup shall have a verification-only mode.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Setup-Host.ps1, HostTools.ps1, Start-RemoteRun.ps1, Run-Endurance.ps1 and Endurance.cs. Verification: tests/Endurance.Tests.ps1, tests/Remote.Tests.ps1 and evidence/remote-workflow-qualification.md. A Linux implementation does not by itself establish Linux execution evidence.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REM-002
TITLE: Identifiable isolated remote result branches
STATEMENT: >>>
The remote workflow shall use a dedicated clean checkout and check publication access before long testing. It shall publish bounded allowlisted evidence to a unique remote-runs/platform-architecture-label/time-source-revision branch, preserving main and source files. Reports shall distinguish full qualification workflow execution from imported endurance-only evidence and preserve failed/unavailable/not-measured outcomes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Start-RemoteRun.ps1 and RemoteQualification.cs. Verification: tests/Remote.Tests.ps1 local bare-Git publication and rejection cases. Bootstrap refuses directories it did not create. No force push, automatic merge or credential-in-URL workflow is provided.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
