[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-001
TITLE: Pinned generated Rust and managed mutation testing
STATEMENT: >>>
The qualification tooling shall run pinned cargo-mutants on owned Rust sources and pinned Stryker.NET on executable managed-client behavior through discoverable real-engine contracts. These maintained frameworks shall be the primary mutation phase, receiving at most half the remaining campaign budget before library-generated property batches. Hand-selected numerical mutations shall remain separate, explicitly selected supplemental regression evidence rather than consuming the default campaign before the frameworks. Rust round-robin shard selection shall be recorded and reproducible from the campaign seed.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs, Endurance.cs, Setup-MutationTools.ps1, dotnet-tools.json, dotnet/Simulator.Client.Tests and shared ConformanceChecks.cs. Verification: evidence/framework-mutation-qualification.md. A candidate inventory is not a tested-mutant count; sharded/time-bounded work is not an exhaustive mutation campaign.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-VERIFY-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: MUT-002
TITLE: Separate mutation outcomes and bounded remote evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutation evidence shall distinguish generated candidates, kills, survivors, uncovered code, timeouts, invalid/compile-error mutants, ignored/pending/unknown categories and unattempted candidates. Framework baseline/infrastructure failures shall remain failures; deadline interruption shall remain partial evidence. Reports shall retain tool pins, tested scope/shard, elapsed budget and native report/log hashes; raw framework artifacts shall remain local. Remote publication shall validate bounded framework-summary hashes and category counts before exporting allowlisted path-free fields.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs, Endurance.cs and RemoteQualification.cs. Verification: tests/FrameworkMutations.Tests.ps1, tests/EnduranceFramework.Tests.ps1, tests/Remote.Tests.ps1, native framework runs and scoped coverage evidence. Timeouts are never counted as test-detected kills, even when a framework score includes them.
<<<
RELATIONS:
