[REQUIREMENT]
UID: END-005
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Suspension-aware campaign deadline and temporary power request
STATEMENT: >>>
Campaign remaining time shall not increase because UTC moves backward or monotonic time pauses across suspension. Child-process and pipe waits shall recheck elapsed deadlines after wake, and successful late batches shall retain replay evidence without adding completed-case counts. A finished budget-exhausted report more than five seconds beyond its budget shall become budget_overrun with a nonzero exit. Five seconds is cleanup allowance, not additional testing time. Windows campaigns shall request system-required power only for their lifetime, record request/release availability and leave persistent power policy unchanged. Explicit sleep and OS policy may override requests; Linux prevention remains unavailable.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Endurance.cs over BCL TimeProvider and Windows PowerCreateRequest/PowerSetRequest/PowerClearRequest. Verification: split-clock self-tests, actual Windows acquire/release probe and synthetic supervisor tests. Windows system events show the original host slept 2026-10-27T10:00:57Z to 13:22:01Z; no five active hours are inferred from the old run. Remote qualification independently rejects over-budget evidence as a passing workflow. Real forced suspension is not injected.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: END-001

